  "summary": [
    "Batch A, family A2 (set-of-edges deletion). Three relations and four graph wrappers now unfold to `GTBase.common.del_es_rel` and `GTBase.common.del_edge_set`: X7, chromatic XE1, extremal XE1, and X191 (`fg_mk_sgraph`). Each frozen copy is checked against the source at 03742d1. Each frozen graph freezes its opaque symmetry and irreflexivity proofs. Each frozen statement goes through frozen copies along its whole affected chain, including XE2, which reaches the extremal XE1 helper across modules. Graph properties move along the identity isomorphism: χ by `chi_diso`, bipartiteness by `bipartite_diso`, balls and diameter by `ball_diso`. X191's blocked row and XE2's solved rows keep their statements. Single-edge deletion (X60, X64, U11) and the dead completion helper are classified and deferred."
  ],
